### Here's&nbsp;Why,&nbsp;Young&nbsp;Academic&nbsp;:fa-orcid: / Full&nbsp;Stack&nbsp;Developer&nbsp;:fa-stack-overflow: / Public&nbsp;Blogger&nbsp;:fa-blog:&nbsp;...

&nbsp;

Want a website that's **secure-by-default**? Easy to update and manage, while hiding the complexity of an underlying version control system, yet giving you its full power when you truly need it?  Instant publication when you want it; smooth, staged branch builds and customizable granular promotions to your production site as it suits your team's preferred workflow.

&nbsp;

If you are tired of the per-seat licensing and per-CPU-cycle choices weighing you down whenever you need to fix a typo, [reach out to us](/contact). If you are in charge of content curation and are pining for a customizable facts database to manage your external links, or if you are a regex-equipped lion tamer for decades of accumulated legacy HTML content, or just someone dissatisfied with the other options on the market and how they function at scale, we have something really special to offer you.

&nbsp;

Never having to deal directly with a version control system, or even a static site generator, on your own personal computer is up to you. The online CMS Editor/IDE is designed and ready for your **browser-only workflow** whenever you are.  In a pinch, even the mobile (browser) interface will get it done, *instantly*.

<div id="lightning">

![Lightning](index.page/lightning)

</div>

<style type="text/css">

div#lightning img {width:100%}

</style>

&nbsp;

Multi-gigabyte source trees are simply no match for it &mdash; full site build durations are measured in *seconds*, not hours and minutes.  The system easily sustains over [`300 MB/s`](features) while processing your sources for full site builds, but given its <span class="text-white">unique, patent-pending dependency management</span> functionality, it almost never needs to resort to them:

&nbsp;

<center>
<span class="text-primary-emphasis"><i class="fa fa-trowel-bricks"></i> <em>We only build what you need built.</em></span>&trade;
</center>

&nbsp;

Taking architectural cues from [David Wheeler's](https://justatheory.com) famous [Bricolage CMS](https://bricolagecms.org/), this [technology](https://iconoclasts.blog/joe/apache-cms) was first invented in late 2010 by [Paul Querna](https://paul.querna.org/articles/2010/10/22/evolution-of-apaches-websites/), Daniel Shahaf, Dave Fisher, and [Joe Schaefer](https://iconoclasts.blog/joe/) as members of the Apache Infrastructure Team. The phrase "JAMstack" was coined years later (2015), by a group unaware of our prior art in this space.  But the [public record](http://web.archive.org/web/20120112045033/http://www.apache.org/dev/cms) is crystal clear, and this new offering by SunStar Systems is testimony to that original legacy and its true open source origins.

&nbsp;

When Apache software project communities were presented with a free choice between using Confluence-backed sites, or using Orion's roots as the Apache CMS, they overwhelmingly chose the Apache CMS. We think you will too, with its vastly improved Orion!

&nbsp;

<h4>Want to give it a quick spin to see how fast and easy it is?</h4>

This website is self-hosted on Orion; all those hot-pink pencil squares [<i class='fa fa-file-pen text-danger'></i>](https://cms.sunstarsys.com/redirect?uri=https://www.sunstarsys.com/index) at the top right are live.  Feel free to poke around and experiment with anything you see!  The only thing you can't do is commit and watch your changes build and deploy; that's restricted to our personnel for obvious reasons.

Our global Point of Presence (POP) network ensures low-latency connections to both Orion &trade; and the end-delivery websites we host.  We are currently on four continents and have a bicoastal presence within the US.  And we're expanding rapidly- next up Africa and East Asia!

&nbsp;

<h3>It's time for a sea change in how you manage and deliver your site to your target audience.</h3>

&nbsp;

Go at your own pace, use as many employees / previews / edits / commits / branches as you like, and only pay for what you *actually use* on our infrastructure. Just bring your own AI enhanced css/javascript framework, perl scripts, and Django Templates, and we will take care of the rest of your setup at no additional charge. We recommend **Bootstrap 5** for css/js styling, as it is what we use internally; but that is entirely up to you.

In addition, all clients have free, template-customizable or javascript-enabled interfaces to our powerful, proprietary `PCRE` search engine.

&nbsp;

<span class="text-white">Want transparency? See for yourself:</span>

Our entire build-system logic for this very website: fewer than 100 lines of code, complete with sophisticated, memoized dependency management that auto-generates multilingual sitemaps, directory indexes, and more.

View the source: [our private source lib tree](https://vcs.sunstarsys.com/repos/svn/public/cms-sites/www.sunstarsys.com/trunk/lib/), or its public [<i class="fa fa-github fa-emoji" title="Github"></i> GitHub mirror](https://github.com/SunStarSys/www/tree/trunk/lib).

The underlying Static Site Generator: open-sourced on GitHub under Apache License 2.0 → @SunStarSys/orion

This isn't marketing spin &mdash; it's verifiable, open engineering heritage dating back to F/OSS innovations pioneered in 2010. Ready to experience a wiki that actually saves time, money, and headaches? [Give us a call or drop us a note](/contact) today.

&nbsp;

